---
source: crates/odx-cli/tests/cli.rs
expression: cmd.render_long_help().to_string()
---
Migrate one addon on the branch `<to>-mig-<addon>`: its history from the source series, the repository's pre-commit fixes, then odoo-lint's upgrade fixes as the `[MIG]` commit

Usage: odx migrate addon [OPTIONS] --to <SERIES> <ADDON>

Arguments:
  <ADDON>
          Addon name

Options:
  -C, --project-dir <DIR>
          Run as if started in DIR

      --to <SERIES>
          Target series

  -c, --config <FILE>
          The pyproject.toml or repos.yaml to use

      --from <SERIES>
          Source series [default: the series before --to]

  -j, --jobs <N>
          Override the number of parallel jobs

      --remote <NAME>
          The remote both series come from [default: `upstream` when it exists, else `origin`]

      --no-pre-commit
          Leave out the repository's pre-commit fixes

      --offline
          Serve forge and index data from the cache only

      --fresh
          Ignore cached data; refresh everything before answering

      --no-squash
          Keep the administrative commits (bots, Weblate) of the history as they are instead of squashing them

      --force
          Migrate even when an open pull request already migrates the addon

      --no-refresh
          Use cached data even when stale

      --open-pr
          Then push the branch and open a draft pull request (`odx migrate pr`)

      --refresh-index
          Rebuild the addon index for the series involved

      --json
          Machine-readable output on stdout

  -v, --verbose...
          Increase log verbosity (repeatable)

  -q, --quiet
          Errors only

  -h, --help
          Print help

  -V, --version
          Print version
